  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dc092c63",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 16. Main Conclusions\n",
    "\n",
    "The comparison of the sixteen classifier-feature strategy combinations shows\n",
    "that feature selection does not universally improve predictive performance.\n",
    "Its effect depends strongly on the classification algorithm.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The strongest overall configuration is the **Neural Network using all\n",
    "  transformed features**, which achieves an F1-score of **0.4738** and a\n",
    "  balanced accuracy of **0.6765**. It therefore provides the best overall\n",
    "  balance between identifying attrition cases and correctly classifying both\n",
    "  target classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **SVM using all features** achieves the highest standard accuracy\n",
    "  (**0.8653**) and precision (**0.8363**). However, its recall is only\n",
    "  **0.2241**, showing that high accuracy alone is misleading for this\n",
    "  imbalanced classification problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "- All three feature-selection strategies reduce the transformed\n",
    "  representation from **51 to 15 features**, corresponding to a dimensionality\n",
    "  reduction of **70.59%**.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Among the reduced representations, the **Wrapper + Neural Network**\n",
    "  configuration obtains the highest F1-score (**0.3919**), closely followed\n",
    "  by the **Multivariate + Neural Network** configuration (**0.3902**).\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **Univariate + Decision Tree** configuration obtains the highest\n",
    "  balanced accuracy among the reduced representations (**0.6347**) and an\n",
    "  F1-score of **0.3809**.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Feature selection has different effects depending on the classifier.\n",
    "  In particular, **K-NN benefits considerably from dimensionality reduction**.\n",
    "  Its F1-score increases from **0.2115** with all features to **0.3146** with\n",
    "  wrapper selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The Decision Tree also benefits moderately from univariate selection, while\n",
    "  the SVM performs consistently worse after dimensionality reduction.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Although the reduced feature subsets do not outperform the strongest\n",
    "  full-feature model, they provide substantially simpler representations while\n",
    "  retaining part of the predictive capability. Therefore, feature selection\n",
    "  introduces a trade-off between predictive performance, dimensionality, and\n",
    "  interpretability.\n",
    "\n",
    "At the original-variable level, several employee characteristics are selected\n",
    "by all three feature-selection strategies:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `BusinessTravel`\n",
    "- `JobInvolvement`\n",
    "- `JobRole`\n",
    "- `MaritalStatus`\n",
    "- `MonthlyIncome`\n",
    "- `OverTime`\n",
    "- `StockOptionLevel`\n",
    "\n",
    "In addition, `Age`, `JobSatisfaction`, `NumCompaniesWorked`, and\n",
    "`TotalWorkingYears` are selected by at least two of the three strategies.\n",
    "\n",
    "These repeated selections suggest that working conditions, job involvement,\n",
    "compensation, professional characteristics, and employment history contain\n",
    "particularly useful information for distinguishing between employees who\n",
    "remain in the company and those who leave.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the complete feature representation provides the strongest predictive\n",
    "performance for this dataset, while feature-selection methods provide more\n",
    "compact and interpretable representations whose effectiveness depends on the\n",
    "classifier being used."
   ]
  }
